THE APPLICATION AS A WHOLE IS CONVEYED UNDER AGPLv3
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Light Host links the JUCE framework, which is dual-licensed under AGPLv3 or
a commercial JUCE licence (see `lib/juce/LICENSE.md`). This project does not
hold a commercial JUCE licence, so it uses JUCE under AGPLv3.

It also builds against the Steinberg ASIO SDK bundled with JUCE, which is
licensed under either the proprietary Steinberg ASIO License or GPL version 3
(see `lib/juce/modules/juce_audio_devices/native/asio/LICENSE.txt`). This
project uses it under GPLv3.

Light Host's own code being GPLv2-*or-later* is what makes this combination
work: it can be taken up to GPLv3, and GPLv3 and AGPLv3 code may be combined.

The practical consequence: while Light Host's own source stays GPLv2-or-later,
any binary distribution of Light Host as a whole is conveyed under the terms of
the GNU Affero General Public License version 3, and recipients of a binary
receive AGPLv3 terms, including its source-availability requirements.

The AGPL version 3 text is in `agpl-3.0.txt`.


EXCEPTION: THE VST2 SDK IS NOT COVERED BY THE ABOVE
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

`lib/vstsdk2.4/` contains headers from the Steinberg VST 2.4 Plug-In SDK.
They are NOT part of the license grant above, are NOT under a GPL-compatible
licence, and are NOT redistributable: the Steinberg VST2 SDK licence prohibits
redistribution, and Steinberg stopped licensing the VST2 SDK in 2018.

Consequently this repository cannot supply complete corresponding source for
the VST2 hosting path under GPL/AGPL terms, and those headers are present here
without a licence permitting their redistribution.

VST2 hosting is compiled in via `JUCE_PLUGINHOST_VST=1` in CMakeLists.txt.
Building with `JUCE_PLUGINHOST_VST=0` and removing `lib/vstsdk2.4/` produces a
tree with no such exception.


